  "limitations": [
    "The duplicate heuristic can falsely match different content having the same case-normalized filename, modification time and length. Skipping is not proof of content identity and never deletes originals.",
    "Source length/modification-time stability remains a heuristic for copying; same-length/same-timestamp concurrent rewrites are not content identity. Ordinary source hashes/timestamps remain unchanged; controlled tests deliberately inject source changes and verify the resulting declared state. Regression hashes are synthetic development assertions, not a runtime hashing requirement.",
    "Inherited HEIC routing and case-only single-directory inventory remain controlled coverage. New duplicate case variants use actual separate source directories. No actual HEIC decode/visual quality or NTFS case-sensitivity changes are claimed.",
    "Drive/UNC checks are lexical only; no live network share, real Pictures, private media or drive-root normalization. Inherited real junction results remain separate from unavailable desktop file-symlink creation and controlled reparse-file coverage.",
    "Native long generated candidates cover the tested Windows paths, not universal long source/final-name support. No hostile-filesystem sandbox, batch atomicity or crash durability is claimed.",
    "No actual Ctrl+C/hard-kill, process lifecycle/timeout cleanup, manual launcher, owner quality acceptance, merge, release or deployment is claimed. M1-T06 full milestone audit, complete corpus/analyzer and later gates remain future tasks."
  ]
